-- title:
--   Unramifiedness of places in a constant field extension
-- statement:
--   Let $K$, $K'$, $F$, $F'$ be fields equipped with algebra maps $K \to K'$, $K' \to F'$, $K \to F'$ forming a tower, and $K \to F$, $F \to F'$ forming a tower with $K \to F'$; assume $K'/K$ is algebraic and separable and $F'/F$ is integral. Two further hypotheses are imposed: `hgen`, that the $F$-subalgebra of $F'$ generated by the image of $K'$ is all of $F'$, so that $F'$ is generated over $F$ by the constants $K'$; and `hconst`, that every $y \in F$ algebraic over $K$ lies in the image of $K$, i.e. $K$ is algebraically closed in $F$. Let $W$ be a place of $F'$ over $K'$, that is, a valuation subring of $F'$ containing the image of $K'$, different from $F'$ itself, and a principal ideal ring. Write $W$ also for the associated place of $F'$ over $K$ obtained by `forgetConstants`: the same valuation subring, which contains the image of $K$ because of the tower $K \subseteq K' \subseteq F'$. The conclusion is that the ramification index of this place over $F$ equals $1$, where that index is by definition the least positive integer $n$ for which some nonzero $f \in F$ has $\operatorname{ord}_W(\operatorname{algebraMap} F F' f) = n$.
--
--   This is the statement that in a constant field extension $F' = F K'$ with $K'/K$ separable algebraic and $K$ algebraically closed in $F$, every place of $F'/K'$ is unramified over its restriction to $F$ (Stichtenoth III.6.3). It is used in the divisor pull-back and push-forward machinery for curves, where the ramification index of such a place cancels in the comparison of order functions before and after forgetting the constants.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicCurve_Place_ramificationIndex_forgetConstants_eq_one_of_isConstantFieldExtension.lean

